  "description": "CR 303.4j whole cards: Crown of the Ages cannot move Setessan Training onto an opponent's creature",
  "note": "CR 303.4j: an Aura the effect tries to attach to something it can't legally enchant doesn't move. Setessan Training's \"Enchant creature you control\" narrows past creature and Crown of the Ages' destination is the bare \"another creature\", so the Crown offers bob's Piker and the move then fails: a failure mode, not a fizzle, and the Aura stays on a legal host through the state-based actions. CR 109.5 fixes that \"you\" as the Aura's controller; alice controls both cards, so this board cannot tell that from the moving effect's. The Haskell test's CR 701.3c stamp reads are dropped: the Training's +1/+0 and trample are commutative here, so its timestamp is unobservable. The control file aims the same activation at alice's own Mammoth, and it moves.",
